properties.description:
Planned 2026-09-27. On SIGTERM or SIGINT, the --http server (a single design or a registry root):
1. stops accepting connections;
2. waits for in-flight requests up to a grace period (configurable, shorter than a container's stop timeout);
3. closes every open design's store and ends its sessions;
4. then exits.
Without this, a deploy that stops the process can end a write mid-way, and every open store is closed by the process dying rather than by its owner.

REALIZED 2026-09-27 in crates/reflow2-mcp/src/drain.rs (chg:an-http-server-drains-before-it-stops-2026-09-27), for every --http server including the shared one. The grace is --shutdown-grace (default 5s), and work is every request that is not a GET, counted until its answer's body is written. It does two things beyond the four above: a write-through change still waiting (--export-to) is written before the stores close, and the server exits 0 with an account of what it did. A second signal exits at once. Checked by ver:a-server-drains-before-it-stops.
